Chapter: F64Probe
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceEffect

 Regression probe for the PTX f64 float path. Codex Real is f64: this
 kernel must emit ld.global.f64 and st.global.f64 for the -f64
 intrinsics, mul.f64 / div.rn.f64 / add.f64 for Real arithmetic,
 mov.f64 for Real literals, setp.gt.f64 for the comparison, .param
 .f64 for the Real-typed helper parameters, and %fd registers
 throughout. test-f64.ps1 asserts those forms are present and that no
 stray .f32 arithmetic appears outside the documented trig sandwich.

Section: Kernels

  gpu-axpy : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  gpu-axpy (xs) (ys) (out) (n) = act
   tid <- thread-idx-x
   if tid < n then f64-axpy-one xs ys out tid
   else 0
  end

  f64-axpy-one : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  f64-axpy-one (xs) (ys) (out) (tid) = act
   x <- device-load-f64 xs tid
   y <- device-load-f64 ys tid
   scaled <- f64-scale x 2.5
   let blended = scaled + y / 4.0
   in let clamped = if blended > 100.0 then 100.0 else blended
   in device-store-f64 out tid clamped
  end

  f64-scale : Real, Real -> [Device] Real
  f64-scale (v) (k) = v * k
